<title>UK: UK not committed to ERM third stage-Clarke.</title>
<headline>UK not committed to ERM third stage-Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer (finance minister) Kenneth Clarke confirmed on Wednesday that Britain was not committed to joining the third stage of European Monetary Union.</p>
<p>&quot;The UK is not committed and cannot be obliged to move to the third stage of European economic and monetary union without a separate decision to do so by the Government and Parliament,&quot; Clarke said in a written reply in parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;The Government's policy remains that no decision will be taken either way on participation in the third stage during the lifetime of the current Parliament because sufficient information to make a full assessment of the implications for the UK will not be available,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
